Qt6 compiler cache
==================

The Qt6 recipe enables ccache with Qt's -ccache configure option.
It sets CCACHE_DIR=/mnt/Storage/scratchpkg/ccache and CCACHE_MAXSIZE=50G.
No shell PATH changes or global compiler optimization changes are needed.
The cache survives Scratch's removal of a package's work directory.

After building Qt6, inspect its cache with:

sudo env CCACHE_DIR=/mnt/Storage/scratchpkg/ccache ccache --show-stats

The first compilation fills the cache. Later compilations can reuse matching
results. Changed source, compiler options, or compiler versions can cause
cache misses. ccache does not cache linking or replace unfinished build files.

The Qt6 recipe preserves its work directory with KEEP_WORK=yes. A normal
Scratch retry still re-extracts sources unless a completed matching package
already exists in Scratch's package cache. To preserve partial compilation,
resume the retained build and package it before running scratch upgrade qt6.

Other recipes use ccache only if they explicitly enable it. Their cache
locations follow ccache's normal defaults unless they set CCACHE_DIR.

Upstream documentation: https://ccache.dev/manual/latest.html
